<?xml version="1.0" ?>

  <!--
    Joint limits corrected by scratch scripts in the mmhand repo.

    little_aa_joint  relabelled by +350.000000 deg (NOT a plain limit shift):
        The raw CAD zero carries 10.000 deg of natural abduction, so the pose
        where the little finger is parallel to Index/Middle/Ring sits at
        theta_raw = -6.108652 rad (-349.999957 deg, measured residual
        0.000003 deg). To put that pose exactly at theta = 0 both the joint
        origin and the limits are rotated by -350/+350 deg:
          origin rpy  0.0 1.396263 -3.141593  ->  -2.992911 1.570796 -2.992912
          limit       [-425, -334] deg        ->  [-75, +16] deg
        The reachable physical arc is unchanged; only the zero label moved.

    thumb_pip_joint  +360.000000 deg -> [-9, +89]
        A full turn, so the origin is untouched and the arc is the same; the
        raw numbers just move back next to the original URDF.

    thumb_cmc_joint   relabelled by +54.000000 deg (option C):
        Same world rotation sense as the original (new +1 deg matches old
        +1 deg within 0.0787 deg), so [0, 54] and the raw [-54, 0] are the two
        opposite 54 deg halves of the same sweep. Option C keeps the CAD's
        physical arc and only moves the zero:
          origin rpy  1.570796 1.570796 0.0  ->  -1.570796 0.628319 -3.141592
          limit       [-54, 0] deg           ->  [0, +54] deg
        theta = 0 now means the raw -54 deg pose (the tightened end).

    index_pip_joint upper limit 101 -> 89 deg
        Every other PIP joint spans exactly 98 deg and 101 is the index DIP
        value, so the CAD value was a typo.

    Links, meshes, axes and every other joint are byte-identical to the CAD
    export. All remaining limits already match the original structure URDF.
  -->
<robot name="mmhand_left_hand_assembly">

